  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Recently I was speaking with a friend on VRChat, and she mentioned that my audio was breaking up.  But, we had no idea whose end the problem was on -- was I failing to transmit audio, or was she failing to receive it?   Even beyond that, on whoever's end the problem was; was it failing to *capture* audio?  Failing to buffer it due to CPU congestion?  Failing to *transmit* it in time due to network congestion?   We had no idea.   Even if it were only opt-in, having somewhere for both users to look to see \"12 outgoing audio packet drops recently\" or whatever to help diagnose who should try tweaking their avatar culling to fix the issue, would be a big leg up...   (I know there's an \"audio sources\" section of the debug interface, but it doesn't look like that describes your own outgoing audio?  And it would probably not be comprehensible to most users anyway, compared to just a nice big ⚠️ symbol somewhere that everyone could check for, to identify whether or not *they're* the one having network or CPU problems at the moment...)",
